The issue was in the `index.js` file, where the `add` function was incorrectly implemented to subtract (`a - b`) instead of adding (`a + b`). This caused the test in `test.js` to fail since it expected `add(2, 2)` to return `4`, but it was returning `0`.

I fixed the bug by changing the implementation of the `add` function in `index.js` from `return a - b` to `return a + b`. After the fix, running `node test.js` completes without any errors, indicating that the test passes.

The change was:
```javascript
// Before:
function add(a, b) { return a - b; }

// After:
function add(a, b) { return a + b; }
```

